        "Problem=coaching-staff hiring is decided by reputation and interviews rather than evidence of player improvement; owner=President of Baseball Operations, GM and manager; decision=hiring or retaining MLB and upper-minors hitting, pitching and catching coaches each October to December, with this offseason's window open now; value at stake=hypothesized as large and recurring because one coach touches many players' outcomes for several seasons, size unknown; mechanism=build a public coach-tenure ledger from press releases and media guides, then estimate each coach's effect on players who changed organizations, comparing the year before arrival with the year after and against matched players who did not move; baseline=network referrals, reputation from players, and interview impressions; software=a coach-attribution tool that ranks candidates with uncertainty intervals and flags coaches whose apparent effect is just regression to the mean.",
        "public_coach_tenure_dataset_completeness",
        "persistence_of_coach_effects_year_over_year",
        "cubs_current_coaching_vacancies_2026_offseason",
        "whether_rival_clubs_use_coach_attribution_models",
        "Problem=pricing players posted from NPB and KBO and signed internationally as free agents; owner=GM, international scouting director and pro scouting director; decision=whether to bid on posted players and how much, during posting windows that usually run November to January; value at stake=potentially large per signing, since these are multi-year major-league contracts, but the number of events per year is small; mechanism=translation models that use public foreign-league stats, including pitch-tracking where it is published, along with age and league-environment adjustments, calibrated on the MLB outcomes of previously posted players; baseline=scouting reports combined with simple ratios of foreign-league stats to MLB stats and agent-driven market comparables; software=a probabilistic translation tool with explicit uncertainty that is updated as each new posting cohort produces MLB results.",
