  ],
  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/0/claim/1",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Arbitration and non-tender triage. Owner: GM and baseball-ops analysts. Decision: tender, non-tender or trade each arbitration-eligible player before the late-November or early-December non-tender deadline, every offseason. Value at stake: each arbitration salary, plus the roster spot and replacement cost. Mechanism: compare the projected arbitration salary (driven by the arbitration process's emphasis on traditional stats) with projected next-season surplus value, and flag players whose run value is mispriced relative to their counting stats. Baseline: a public projection system plus a public arbitration salary estimate, with a gut call on borderline cases. Software: a ledger that ranks every arbitration-eligible player on the roster by projected surplus over a replacement acquirable at similar cost. Retrospective test: public arbitration salaries and public next-season performance.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/0/claim/2",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Arbitration outcomes reward counting stats more than run value, so a systematic gap between salary and value exists and persists.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/0/claim/3",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Non-tender decisions involve enough marginal cases each year for better ranking to change outcomes.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/0/claim/4",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "UNKNOWN",
      "text": "cubs_2027_arbitration_eligible_list",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/0/claim/5",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "UNKNOWN",
      "text": "public_arbitration_salary_estimate_accuracy_history",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/0/claim/6",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Club-option and qualifying-offer decisions. Owner: GM and president of baseball operations. Decision: exercise or decline club and mutual options shortly after the World Series, and extend or withhold qualifying offers by the early-November deadline. Value at stake: option salaries, qualifying-offer salary exposure, and draft-pick compensation. Mechanism: estimate the probability that a qualifying offer is accepted and the player's free-agent market value from public contract history and the player's profile (age, injury record, agent). Baseline: accept the option if projected value exceeds its cost, and assume most qualifying offers are declined. Software: an acceptance-probability model and an option valuation calculator that includes the value of the compensation pick. Retrospective test: public qualifying-offer acceptance history and public contract data.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/0/claim/7",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Qualifying-offer acceptance is predictable from public features beyond what the simple \"most decline\" rule already captures.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/0/claim/8",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "The number of option and qualifying-offer cases per year is enough to make this recurring rather than occasional.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/0/claim/9",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "UNKNOWN",
      "text": "qualifying_offer_amount_2026",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/0/claim/10",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "UNKNOWN",
      "text": "cubs_pending_option_decisions_2026",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/0/claim/11",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Free-agent contract pricing and winner's-curse correction. Owner: GM, president of baseball operations and ownership. Decision: bid levels and contract structures (years, opt-outs, deferrals) during the November-to-February signing window. Value at stake: the largest discretionary payroll commitments of each offseason. Mechanism: the club that wins an auction tends to overpay, so the club adjusts its bids for that, models aging curves with uncertainty bands, and prices opt-outs as options that benefit the player. Baseline: a public projection system, a dollars-per-WAR rule and crowdsourced contract estimates. Software: a contract valuation tool that discounts deferrals, prices opt-outs and estimates rival demand. Retrospective test: public contracts against realized public WAR.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/0/claim/12",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "The dollars-per-WAR baseline mis-states the value of opt-outs and deferrals by enough to matter.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/0/claim/13",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Clubs are already sophisticated here, so the advantage may be small. This may be an area where clubs are already ahead of public tools.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/0/claim/14",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "UNKNOWN",
      "text": "cubs_2027_payroll_budget",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/0/claim/15",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "UNKNOWN",
      "text": "public_dollars_per_war_estimate_stability",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/0/claim/16",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Pre-arbitration extension timing. Owner: GM and ownership. Decision: when to offer early extensions to young players, typically in spring training or the offseason, every year. Value at stake: future arbitration and free-agent years bought at a discount. Mechanism: offer when public performance noise has inflated the player's risk discount but underlying skill indicators are stable. Baseline: extend after a strong breakout season, or extend top-ranked prospects. Software: an extension-timing model that compares the player's leverage curve with a skill-stability estimate. Retrospective test: public extension terms against counterfactual arbitration paths.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/0/claim/17",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Public underlying metrics stabilize earlier than surface results, so the timing edge is real.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/0/claim/18",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "The player's and agent's willingness to accept is not mainly driven by information outside the model.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/0/claim/19",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "UNKNOWN",
      "text": "cubs_pre_arbitration_core_list",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/0/claim/20",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Prospect valuation in trades. Owner: GM and pro-scouting director. Decision: which prospects to trade and which to acquire, at the July deadline and in offseason trades, every year. Value at stake: future controllable surplus that moves in each trade. Mechanism: calibrate public prospect rankings and stat lines against later outcomes to find which ranking tiers and profiles the market systematically overvalues or undervalues. Baseline: trade partners and media price prospects by public top-100 lists and organizational rank. Software: a model that converts ranking history into an outcome probability, applied to trade candidates. Retrospective test: archived public rankings against realized MLB careers.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/0/claim/21",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Other clubs price prospects off consensus rankings enough for a calibration gap to exist.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/0/claim/22",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Internal club data makes this edge smaller than public data suggests. Clubs may already be ahead here.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/0/claim/23",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "UNKNOWN",
      "text": "archived_public_prospect_ranking_availability_and_terms",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
