    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/0/claim/24",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Draft bonus-pool allocation. Owner: amateur scouting director and GM. Decision: whom to take at each slot and how to distribute the bonus pool across under-slot and over-slot signings, in the July draft, every year. Value at stake: the full annual draft pool and the early-round surplus it buys. Mechanism: model signability and the expected value per bonus dollar by player type (college or high school, hitter or pitcher) using public draft history. Baseline: take the best player available on the club's board at slot. Software: a pool-allocation optimizer constrained by public slot values and signing rules. Retrospective test: public draft, bonus and outcome records.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/0/claim/25",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "The value per bonus dollar differs reliably by player type, and the market has not already arbitraged that difference away.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/0/claim/26",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Clubs already model this extensively, so the marginal edge from public data may be small. Clubs may already be ahead here.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/0/claim/27",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "UNKNOWN",
      "text": "cubs_2027_draft_position_and_pool",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/0/claim/28",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Catcher valuation shift under automated ball-strike challenges. Owner: GM and pro-scouting director. Decision: trading for, signing and assigning roster time to catchers each offseason. Value at stake: the share of catcher value that came from pitch framing, which may shrink if challenges reverse framed calls. Mechanism: the market may keep paying for framing value that has partly disappeared, while undervaluing blocking, throwing and offense. Baseline: public catcher defensive leaderboards that include framing runs. Software: a model that re-weights catcher value by expected challenge reversal rates. Retrospective test: limited, using whichever public seasons and leagues used the challenge system.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/0/claim/29",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "MLB's 2026 rules include a ball-strike challenge system that reduces framing value. This must be verified.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/0/claim/30",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "This is distinct from the already-explored challenge-strategy family because it concerns roster valuation, not in-game challenges.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/0/claim/31",
