    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/1/claim/1",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/1",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Arbitration filing-number estimation. Owner: front office baseball operations and legal or arbitration staff. Decision: whether to file or exchange salary figures, and at what number, for each arbitration-eligible player. Timing: once a year at the January exchange deadline, with settlement talks before hearings. Value at stake: the gap between the filed number and the eventual salary, repeated across several players a year and carried into later arbitration years. Mechanism: model how hearing panels have weighed public criteria such as platform-year counting stats, service class and comparable-player salaries, then choose a number that is likely to win or to anchor settlement well. Baseline: published public arbitration projections plus comparables picked by hand. Software: a comparable-retrieval and outcome model trained on public historical filings, settlements and hearing results, tested retrospectively against past exchanges.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/1/claim/2",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/1",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Enough historical filed figures and hearing outcomes are public to train and test a model better than existing public projections.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/1/claim/3",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/1",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Panels weigh traditional counting stats more than modern metrics, so the reasoning differs from player-value modeling.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/1/claim/4",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/1",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Clubs are probably already sophisticated here, so the edge may be small, and the improvement must be measured against public projections rather than against no model.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/1/claim/5",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/1",
      "kind": "UNKNOWN",
      "text": "count_of_public_arbitration_hearing_outcomes_by_year",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/1/claim/6",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/1",
      "kind": "UNKNOWN",
      "text": "cubs_arbitration_eligible_players_2027",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/1/claim/7",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/1",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Tender and non-tender decisions. Owner: general manager and president of baseball operations. Decision: tender or non-tender each arbitration-eligible player. Timing: the November non-tender deadline. Value at stake: one projected arbitration salary per marginal player against the replacement cost of similar players on the open market afterward. Mechanism: compare the projected arbitration cost with the market price of comparable non-tendered players, using public signing data from past offseasons. Baseline: a rule of tendering unless projected salary clearly exceeds expected value. Software: a model that pairs projected arbitration salary with the historical post-non-tender market for similar profiles.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/1/claim/8",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/1",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Public signing terms for non-tendered players are complete enough to estimate the replacement market.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/1/claim/9",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/1",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "The decision is coupled to 40-man roster space, which overlaps an explored family and must be separated in any test.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/1/claim/10",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/1",
      "kind": "UNKNOWN",
      "text": "historical_nontender_resigning_price_distribution",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/1/claim/11",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/1",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Qualifying offer extend-or-decline and signing QO-tagged free agents. Owner: front office leadership and ownership for the budget. Decision: whether to extend a qualifying offer to the club's own free agents, and whether a QO-tagged free agent is worth the draft-pick and bonus-pool forfeit. Timing: in the days after the World Series, and then throughout the free-agent period. Value at stake: one-year salary at the QO amount, plus draft compensation picks and their slot bonus values. Mechanism: estimate acceptance probability from public QO history, and price the forfeited picks using historical draft-slot outcomes. Baseline: offer QOs only to clearly top free agents, and treat forfeited picks as a flat cost. Software: an acceptance-probability model plus a pick-value curve, tested on public QO decisions since the system began.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/1/claim/12",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/1",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "QO rules and compensation tiers may change in the next collective bargaining agreement, which could invalidate historical training data.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/1/claim/13",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/1",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "The pick-value curve can be estimated from public draft and career outcome data without private grades.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/1/claim/14",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/1",
      "kind": "UNKNOWN",
      "text": "cubs_2026_free_agents_qo_eligible",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/1/claim/15",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/1",
      "kind": "UNKNOWN",
      "text": "next_cba_qo_rules",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/1/claim/16",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/1",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Labor-agreement scenario planning. Owner: ownership, business operations and baseball operations jointly. Decision: offseason commitment timing, such as signing multi-year deals before or after any labor resolution and structuring contract years around possible changes to the luxury tax or revenue rules. Timing: this offseason, and at each future agreement expiration. Value at stake: multi-year payroll commitments, plus taxes or penalties under rules that could change. Mechanism: run contract structures against several plausible rule scenarios, using public reporting on bargaining positions. Baseline: wait and see, with a qualitative judgment by leadership. Software: a scenario engine that recomputes the luxury-tax payroll calculation, compensation rules and service-time effects under different rule sets.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/1/claim/17",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/1",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "The current collective bargaining agreement expires around this offseason, which needs verification.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/1/claim/18",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/1",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "This decision is rare rather than recurring, so a retrospective test is weak (past expirations offer few samples).",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/1/claim/19",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/1",
      "kind": "UNKNOWN",
      "text": "cba_expiration_date_verified",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/1/claim/20",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/1",
      "kind": "UNKNOWN",
      "text": "cubs_luxury_tax_payroll_2027",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/1/claim/21",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/1",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Club option and player opt-out forecasting. Owner: front office. Decision: exercise or decline the club's own options, and anticipate opt-out exercises by players on the roster or on target lists. Timing: shortly after the World Series each year. Value at stake: the option salary against the market replacement price, often seven figures. Mechanism: compare the option price with the estimated open-market price for the same projected performance, using public contract and projection data. Baseline: exercise the option if the player was productive last season. Software: a market-price estimator for one-year deals, tested against public option decisions and the contracts players later signed.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/1/claim/22",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/1",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Most option decisions are already obvious, so the model matters only at the margin and could be unnecessary.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/1/claim/23",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/1",
      "kind": "UNKNOWN",
      "text": "cubs_club_options_2027",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/1/claim/24",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/1",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Trade-deadline buy, sell or hold valuation. Owner: president of baseball operations and general manager. Decision: whether to add, subtract or stand pat, and how much prospect value to spend. Timing: each July before the deadline. Value at stake: the change in playoff probability per added win, times postseason revenue and the value of playing in October, against the surplus value of the prospects traded. Mechanism: the value of a marginal win is nonlinear in the standings, and public playoff-odds simulations can show where a deadline win is unusually valuable or nearly worthless. Baseline: use a public playoff-odds percentage, with buy or sell judged by feel. Software: a model that turns public odds simulations into a marginal-win value curve, combined with a public-data model of prospect surplus value, tested on historical deadline moves against season outcomes.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/1/claim/25",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/1",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Postseason revenue per series can be estimated from public sources, since actual Cubs revenue is private.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/1/claim/26",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/1",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "The retrospective test is confounded because counterfactual seasons are unobservable, so only the decision rule can be evaluated against simulated outcomes.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/1/claim/27",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/1",
      "kind": "UNKNOWN",
      "text": "postseason_revenue_per_round_public_estimate",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/1/claim/28",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/1",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Draft bonus-pool allocation and signability. Owner: the scouting director and amateur scouting department. Decision: how to distribute bonus-pool dollars across picks, including under-slot deals early in exchange for over-slot deals later. Timing: each July draft and signing deadline. Value at stake: the expected surplus value of draftees, with penalties for exceeding the pool. Mechanism: public data on slot values, signed bonuses and later outcomes show whether money moved to later rounds produced more value than spending it at the top picks. Baseline: take the best player available near slot and take conventional senior signs to save money. Software: an allocation optimizer that uses public bonus and outcome history, tested on past drafts.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/1/claim/29",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/1",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Public bonus data are complete enough, and the outcome horizon is long enough, for a test (draftees take years to mature).",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/1/claim/30",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/1",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Clubs are already sophisticated at pool management, so the edge may be small.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/1/claim/31",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/1",
      "kind": "UNKNOWN",
      "text": "public_bonus_data_completeness_by_year",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/1/claim/32",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/1",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Pre-arbitration extension timing and pricing. Owner: front office and ownership. Decision: which young controllable players to offer early extensions, and at what guarantee. Timing: often in spring training, and occasionally in other windows. Value at stake: tens of millions in arbitration and free-agent years bought out at a discount, against the risk of injury or decline. Mechanism: use public history of early extensions and the players' later outcomes to estimate when the risk-adjusted price favors the club. Baseline: match public comparable extensions. Software: a model linking service time, performance trajectory and comparable deals to fair-value ranges, tested on public extensions and later career outcomes.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/1/claim/33",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/1",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "The sample of public extensions with matured outcomes is large enough for a test.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/1/claim/34",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/1",
      "kind": "UNKNOWN",
      "text": "cubs_extension_candidates_2027",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/1/claim/35",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/1",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Areas where software is likely unnecessary, or where clubs are likely already ahead. These include dynamic ticket pricing (vendor platforms already exist), in-game bullpen leverage and pinch-hit decisions (clubs have in-house models), free-agent aging curves (well studied publicly and privately), and international amateur signings (deals are typically agreed years ahead, before public information is useful).",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/1/claim/36",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/1",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Vendor pricing tools and in-house in-game models are already widespread across clubs.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/1/claim/37",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/1",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "International agreements made years in advance leave little room for decision-time software.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/1/claim/38",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/1",
      "kind": "UNKNOWN",
      "text": "cubs_existing_internal_tooling",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/2/claim/1",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/2",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Arbitration salary forecasting and file-or-settle strategy. Owner: front office baseball operations and legal or payroll staff. Decision: each winter, before the arbitration filing deadline, set exchange figures and decide which cases to settle or take to hearing (file-and-trial posture). Value at stake: multi-year payroll effects, because arbitration salaries compound across a player's arb years. Mechanism: comparable-player retrieval from public arbitration outcomes, using conventional arb criteria (playing time, counting stats, awards) instead of modern metrics, could estimate both the hearing win probability and the midpoint. Baseline: the agent-style comparables used by club arbitration staff, plus public projection sites. Software: a model trained on historical public filing figures and hearing results that outputs a recommended filing figure and a settle-or-hearing probability.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/2/claim/2",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/2",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Public historical filing figures and hearing outcomes are complete enough to train and backtest on.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/2/claim/3",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/2",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Arbitration panels' reliance on traditional stats is stable enough over time that past outcomes predict future ones.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/2/claim/4",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/2",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Most clubs already run comparable systems, so any edge may be at the margin of the settle-or-hearing decision rather than in salary prediction.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/2/claim/5",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/2",
      "kind": "UNKNOWN",
      "text": "cubs_arbitration_eligible_players_2027",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/2/claim/6",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/2",
      "kind": "UNKNOWN",
      "text": "cubs_file_and_trial_policy",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/2/claim/7",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/2",
      "kind": "UNKNOWN",
      "text": "public_hearing_outcome_dataset_coverage",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/2/claim/8",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/2",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Non-tender and tender decision support. Owner: front office. Decision: at the annual non-tender deadline (late November or early December), choose which arbitration-eligible and pre-arb players to tender. Value at stake: roster spots and projected arbitration salaries, weighed against replacement cost on the open market. Mechanism: compare each player's projected arb salary with the projected market price of an equivalent replacement, using public projections and post-deadline signing prices from past years. Baseline: front-office judgment, plus a simple rule such as \"tender if projected WAR × market $/WAR exceeds projected arb salary.\" Software: a backtest of past non-tender classes showing whether non-tendered players were later signed cheaply and performed, which calibrates the replacement-cost curve.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/2/claim/9",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/2",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Non-tendered players' later contracts and performance are publicly recoverable for a retrospective test.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/2/claim/10",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/2",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "The simple $/WAR rule may already capture most of the value, mirroring the R001 finding; this should be tested before building anything elaborate.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/2/claim/11",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/2",
      "kind": "UNKNOWN",
      "text": "market_dollars_per_war_2026_offseason",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/2/claim/12",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/2",
      "kind": "UNKNOWN",
      "text": "historical_nontender_class_outcomes",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/2/claim/13",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/2",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Qualifying offer extend-or-decline and compensation-pick valuation. Owner: front office and ownership. Decision: in the days after the World Series, decide whether to extend the qualifying offer to eligible pending free agents, and value the draft compensation forgone when signing other clubs' QO-tagged free agents. Value at stake: a one-year salary at the QO amount, set against compensation-pick value and bonus pool consequences. Mechanism: model acceptance probability from public historical QO acceptances by player age, platform-year performance, and market conditions, and value compensation picks using public draft-slot outcome histories. Baseline: extend the QO to any player expected to beat it on the open market. Software: an acceptance-probability model plus a draft-pick value curve, backtested on public QO history since the system began.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/2/claim/14",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/2",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "The number of historical QO decisions is small, so model confidence may be low.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/2/claim/15",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/2",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Compensation rules depend on revenue-sharing and luxury-tax status, which must be verified for the Cubs for each season.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/2/claim/16",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/2",
      "kind": "UNKNOWN",
      "text": "cubs_qo_eligible_players_2026",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/2/claim/17",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/2",
      "kind": "UNKNOWN",
      "text": "qualifying_offer_amount_2026",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/2/claim/18",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/2",
      "kind": "UNKNOWN",
      "text": "cubs_cbt_status_2026",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/2/claim/19",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/2",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Pre-arbitration extension timing. Owner: front office. Decision: recurring each spring and offseason, decide when to offer team-friendly extensions to young players, and at what guarantee. Value at stake: potentially large surplus over a contract's term, but with concentrated injury and performance risk. Mechanism: estimate the expected surplus of extending now versus waiting a year, using public extension terms and subsequent player outcomes. Baseline: extending when a player shows early success, priced off recent comparable extensions. Software: a comparable-extension database with an outcome-weighted surplus estimate and an option-value comparison of waiting.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/2/claim/20",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/2",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Public reporting of extension terms, including options and escalators, is accurate and complete enough to value them.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/2/claim/21",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/2",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Player willingness to accept an extension is not observable, so the model can only inform the offer side.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/2/claim/22",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/2",
      "kind": "UNKNOWN",
      "text": "cubs_pre_arb_core_players_2027",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/2/claim/23",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/2",
      "kind": "UNKNOWN",
      "text": "public_extension_terms_dataset_completeness",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/2/claim/24",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/2",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Trade-deadline buy, sell, or hold timing. Owner: front office and ownership. Decision: each June to July, decide whether to acquire or move players, and how aggressively. Value at stake: playoff probability changes, playoff revenue, and prospect capital spent. Mechanism: estimate the marginal playoff-odds gain per added win as a function of standings position, using public playoff-odds histories, and compare it with the public prospect-value cost of acquisitions. Baseline: public playoff odds plus a \"buy if contending\" rule. Software: a marginal-value calculator that is retrospectively testable against past deadline deals and actual postseason qualification.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/2/claim/25",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/2",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Public playoff-odds models are calibrated well enough to serve as inputs.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/2/claim/26",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/2",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Most clubs already run playoff-odds-based deadline models, so the edge may be small.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/2/claim/27",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/2",
      "kind": "UNKNOWN",
      "text": "cubs_ownership_payroll_constraints",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/2/claim/28",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/2",
      "kind": "UNKNOWN",
      "text": "playoff_revenue_per_round_public_estimate",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/2/claim/29",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/2",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Amateur draft bonus pool allocation (over-slot and under-slot strategy). Owner: amateur scouting director and front office. Decision: each July draft, choose picks and negotiate bonuses within the assigned bonus pool. Value at stake: long-term prospect value from many picks, constrained by the pool and penalties. Mechanism: public draft histories with bonuses and later MLB outcomes could estimate the value of shifting dollars from early picks to later over-slot signings. Baseline: picking the best available player at roughly slot value, guided by consensus public draft rankings. Software: a bonus-allocation optimizer using historical outcome curves by player type (college or prep, pitcher or hitter) and bonus.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/2/claim/30",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/2",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Public bonus and outcome data cover enough years since the bonus-pool system began to estimate outcome curves.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/2/claim/31",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/2",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Outcome labels need many years to mature, which limits backtests on recent drafts.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/2/claim/32",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/2",
      "kind": "UNKNOWN",
      "text": "cubs_2027_draft_position",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/2/claim/33",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/2",
      "kind": "UNKNOWN",
      "text": "cubs_2027_bonus_pool",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/2/claim/34",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/2",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "International amateur bonus pool allocation. Owner: international scouting director. Decision: each signing period (opening in mid-January under current rules), allocate the pool across signings and trades of pool space. Value at stake: long-horizon prospect value. Mechanism: public signing records and later outcomes could estimate whether spreading the pool beats concentrating it on top prospects. Baseline: commitments to top-ranked prospects agreed years in advance. Software: a historical outcome analysis by bonus tier.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/2/claim/35",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/2",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Commitments are effectively made years ahead, so software would affect only the residual allocation.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/2/claim/36",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/2",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Very long outcome lags, together with any international draft changes under the next CBA, may make backtests obsolete.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/2/claim/37",
