      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/baseline/0/2",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Dynamic ticket pricing and secondary-market monitoring. Owner: business operations and ticketing. Decision: daily price adjustments in the months before each home game. Value at stake: ticket revenue across a full home schedule, which matters to the business but is not a baseball-performance advantage. Mechanism: forecast demand from opponent, weather, day of week, promotions, and secondary-market prices. Baseline: vendor dynamic-pricing tools, which most clubs already use. Software: a demand model tested on public secondary-market price histories.",
