      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Problem=pre-arbitration extension timing; owner=GM and baseball operations contract staff; decision=whether, when, and at what price to offer long-term extensions to players with under three years of service, recurring each spring and offseason; value at stake=multi-year salary commitments plus surplus value if the player outperforms the deal; mechanism=model a player's arbitration salary path and free-agent value under uncertainty using public performance, service time and past extension terms, then price the option value of waiting one more season; baseline=negotiate from recent comparable extensions and agent anchors; intervention=a retrospective simulator that replays past public extensions against \"wait one year\" counterfactuals.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
