      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/0",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Problem=salary arbitration filing and hearing strategy; owner=baseball operations and legal or contract staff; decision=the filing number and whether to go \"file-and-trial\" or settle, made each January; value at stake=individual awards across the arbitration-eligible roster, plus effects on later raises because arbitration salaries compound; mechanism=predict the panel outcome from the public history of hearings, filing midpoints and the platform statistics panels historically reward, and quantify the expected value of settling versus a hearing; baseline=midpoint settlement using comparables chosen by staff; intervention=a hearing-outcome predictor tested on public hearing records.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
