      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Problem=amateur draft bonus pool allocation; owner=amateur scouting director; decision=draft order and bonus allocation across the first ten rounds, made each July; value at stake=pool dollars, the risk of exceeding the pool, and value from later rounds; mechanism=model signability and likely bonus relative to slot from public signals such as college eligibility year, prior draft status and public commitments, so the club can spend under slot early and redirect money to later high-ceiling picks; baseline=board ranking plus area scout signability notes; intervention=a signability and bonus predictor backtested on public draft bonus data.",
