      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Problem=waiver claim and designated-for-assignment pickup decisions; owner=pro scouting and GM; decision=whether to claim or trade for players designated for assignment, happening throughout the year in a recurring stream; value at stake=low acquisition cost per player but high frequency, with occasional breakout players; mechanism=rank DFA players at the time of designation using only public data available then, such as underlying contact quality, velocity trends and option status, and target players whose skills are undervalued by their surface results; baseline=claim if the player fits a 40-man need and has recent MLB time; intervention=a dated-snapshot ranker backtested on public transaction logs.",
