      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Problem=day-game-heavy home scheduling effects on player performance; owner=manager and performance staff; decision=rest days and lineup choices around day games after night games, made weekly in season; value at stake=small per game but recurring across the season; mechanism=estimate from public game logs whether performance drops in day-after-night games and whether rest timing reduces the drop; baseline=veteran rest by feel and fixed rest rotations; intervention=a rest-scheduling recommender tested on public game-level history.",
