      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Qualifying offer decisions; owner: GM/president of baseball operations; decision: whether to extend a qualifying offer to each eligible departing free agent, made yearly in the days after the World Series; value at stake: a one-year salary at the QO amount if accepted versus a compensation draft pick if declined; mechanism: estimate acceptance probability and market AAV from public signals at decision time (age, recent WAR, injury history, agent, market depth at the position) instead of a binary rule; baseline: offer when expected market AAV clearly exceeds the QO amount; software: a calibrated acceptance and market-value model backtested on public QO outcomes since the system began.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
