      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Postseason series roster construction; owner: baseball operations plus manager; decision: choosing the 26-man roster for each playoff round, made in the days before each series; value at stake: elimination games where a single roster slot such as a pinch runner, an extra reliever, or a platoon bat can swing leverage; mechanism: simulate the series using the opponent's projected starters, bullpen depth, and handedness mix to value marginal slots; baseline: carry the regular-season active roster with minor swaps based on health and intuition; software: a series-specific roster optimizer, backtested by replaying public postseason rosters against their alternatives.",
