      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Coaching hire evaluation; owner: president of baseball operations and manager; decision: hiring or retaining major-league and upper-minors hitting, pitching, and assistant coaches, made mainly in October and November; value at stake: staff who may influence many players at once across multiple seasons; mechanism: estimate a coach-associated change in player outcomes (for example plate discipline or pitch-mix shifts) from public data across all clubs when coaches move between organizations; baseline: reputation, referrals, and interviews; software: a coach-movement panel built from public staff announcements linked to player-level Statcast changes, with controls for aging and regression.",
