      "text": "Rotation sequencing around off-days; owner: manager and pitching coach; decision: whether to keep a strict rotation order, skip a starter, or insert a sixth starter around scheduled off-days, made weekly during the season; value at stake: allocation of starts among starters of different quality, plus fatigue costs; mechanism: model the quality gained by giving the best starters more starts against public evidence of rest-day effects on velocity and results; baseline: a fixed five-man order, with skips only for injury; software: a schedule-aware start allocator, backtested on public game logs and Statcast velocity by days of rest.",
