      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Problem=managing starters around expected rain delays at a home park without a roof; owner=manager, pitching coach and head of game operations; decision=on game days with uncertain weather, whether to start the scheduled starter, use an opener or delay the start, decided in the hours before first pitch; value at stake=hypothesized as modest per event but recurring, through avoided wasted starts and short outings that tax the bullpen; mechanism=combine public precipitation forecasts with historical delay records to estimate the probability of a delay longer than a starter can wait out; baseline=staff judgment plus the umpire crew and league's consultation on weather; software=a delay-risk forecast linked to a rule for choosing the starter.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
