      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/3",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Problem=postseason roster construction for short series; owner=manager, GM and analytics staff; decision=choosing the 26-man roster per round in October, including the count of pitchers versus position players and specialist slots such as pinch runner or third catcher; value=high-leverage innings concentrated in very few games; mechanism=simulating series-specific opponent handedness, off days and starter usage may reveal that the marginal 13th pitcher is worth less than a bench bat or runner; baseline=carry the regular-season structure with the top pitchers; intervention=a series simulator that scores roster variants using public schedules, opponent splits and historical postseason usage.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/3/claim/8",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/3",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Postseason sample sizes are too small for direct outcome backtesting, so validation would depend on simulator calibration rather than observed wins.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
