      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/3",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Problem=international amateur bonus-pool allocation; owner=international scouting director; decision=distributing the annual signing pool across prospects at the January signing period, with verbal agreements made years earlier; value=the full annual pool plus long-tail prospect value; mechanism=public prospect rankings and published bonuses could show whether value per dollar is higher in concentrated top signings or in spread mid-tier signings; baseline=commit to a few top-ranked players early; intervention=a portfolio model trained on public signing-class bonuses and eventual prospect-list or MLB outcomes.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
