      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/3",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "This may overlap with already explored attribution families and should be checked for duplication.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/3/claim/23",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/3",
      "kind": "UNKNOWN",
      "text": "coach_effect_identifiability",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/3/claim/24",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/3",
      "kind": "UNKNOWN",
      "text": "public_coaching_staff_history_completeness",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/3/claim/25",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/3",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Problem=early-season weather and postponement exposure at Wrigley; owner=business operations together with the league; decision=managing April and May home-date risk, including ticket and promotion plans and pitcher scheduling around likely postponements; value=lost gate revenue, doubleheader workload and staff-planning costs; mechanism=public historical weather and postponement records could quantify risk by date to inform promotion placement and rotation contingency planning; baseline=static calendar planning; intervention=a date-risk calendar and contingency planner.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/3/claim/26",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/3",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Schedule and postponement authority sits largely with the league, which limits club leverage.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/3/claim/27",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/3",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "The business side likely already uses commercial weather services, so software may be unnecessary here.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/3/claim/28",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/3",
      "kind": "UNKNOWN",
      "text": "club_control_over_postponement_decisions",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/3/claim/29",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/3",
      "kind": "UNKNOWN",
      "text": "historical_wrigley_postponement_counts",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/3/claim/30",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/3",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Problem=where software is unnecessary; owner=analytics leadership; decision=annual triage of which tooling to build; value=staff time saved; mechanism=explicitly drop areas where clubs are already ahead or rules already dominate, such as concession demand forecasting, dynamic ticket pricing done by vendors, and minor-league free-agent triage; baseline=build tools by request; intervention=a short scoring rubric rating each candidate on value size, public-signal edge and backtestability.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/3/claim/31",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/3",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Ticketing and concessions forecasting at MLB clubs is already mature and vendor-supported, so a marginal internal build adds little.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/3/claim/32",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/3",
      "kind": "UNKNOWN",
      "text": "club_existing_tooling_inventory",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/4/claim/1",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/4",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Problem family: estimating the marginal value of coaching and player-development staff hires. This is a decision family not covered by the explored list.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/4/claim/2",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/4",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Decision owner: the President of Baseball Operations and GM, with input from the farm director for minor-league staff.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/4/claim/3",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/4",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Recurring decision: hiring, retaining or replacing MLB coaches, such as hitting, pitching, catching and bench coaches.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/4/claim/4",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/4",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Timing: each October through December, and staff turnover across MLB clusters in the weeks after clubs are eliminated. Early October 2026 is inside this window for the Cubs.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/4/claim/5",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/4",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Recurring decision: filling minor-league coordinator and affiliate coach roles each winter. These hires shape many player-seasons at once.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/4/claim/6",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/4",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Value at stake (hypothesis): a coach touches every player on the staff or lineup for multiple seasons. A real coach effect would therefore compound across far more player-seasons than any single roster move.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/4/claim/7",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/4",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Value at stake (hypothesis): coaching salaries are small compared with player payroll, so a good evaluation could have high leverage per dollar if true coach effects exist.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/4/claim/8",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/4",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Simple baseline a club already uses: hire by reputation, playing career, network referrals, interviews, and the outcomes of the coach's prior team.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/4/claim/9",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/4",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Mechanism of advantage: public team and staff directories, media transaction reports and Baseball-Reference coaching records can be joined to player-level public metrics. This builds a coach-player linkage panel.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/4/claim/10",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/4",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Mechanism of advantage: use movement-based identification. Track the same players under different coaches, and the same coaches with different players. This separates coach effects from player aging and talent.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/4/claim/11",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/4",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Mechanism of advantage: the model would estimate within-player changes after a coaching change, compared against matched players whose coaches did not change. It would use public outcome metrics such as chase rate, zone contact, pitch-mix shifts and walk rate.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/4/claim/12",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/4",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Software intervention: a coach-candidate dossier generator. For each candidate it would report the before/after trajectories of players they coached, with uncertainty intervals, matched controls and sample-size warnings.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/4/claim/13",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/4",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Software intervention: a retrospective test. Freeze data as of each past offseason, rank the coaching hires made that winter, and check whether the rankings predicted the next one to two seasons of player-change metrics better than the prior-team-outcome baseline.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/4/claim/14",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/4",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Unconventional extension: treat staff as a scarce market. Flag undervalued coaches whose players improved but whose teams lost, since a team-record baseline would systematically overlook them.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/4/claim/15",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/4",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Coach effects on player outcomes are large enough and persistent enough to detect above noise. This is the central challenge, and the result may well be a null.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/4/claim/16",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/4",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Public staff assignment data is complete and accurately dated enough to build a linkage panel. Mid-season title changes and shared roles may blur attribution.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/4/claim/17",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/4",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Player improvement after a coaching change is not dominated by confounders that public data cannot separate. Examples include regression to the mean, front-office technology, private biomechanics programs, and the same front office hiring both the player and the coach.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/4/claim/18",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/4",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Hitting and pitching coaches control enough of player development to deserve credit. Many clubs spread instruction across analysts, coordinators and private trainers, so attribution may be meaningless.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/4/claim/19",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/4",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "The number of coach moves per year gives enough independent events for a retrospective test. Small N could make any ranking statistically indistinguishable from the reputation baseline.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/4/claim/20",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/4",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Clubs that already analyze coaches internally with private data are likely ahead of a public-data model. Software may then add little beyond organizing candidate research.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/4/claim/21",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/4",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Interpersonal fit, communication and clubhouse trust may dominate a coach's value and resist public measurement. A quantitative dossier might mislead more than it informs if over-weighted.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/4/claim/22",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/4",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Software may be unnecessary if the binding constraint is candidate availability or salary competition rather than evaluation quality.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/4/claim/23",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/4",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Minor-league staff effects might be more detectable than MLB effects because the player samples are larger. However, public minor-league tracking data may be too thin or too recent to support this.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/4/claim/24",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/4",
      "kind": "UNKNOWN",
      "text": "magnitude_of_true_mlb_coach_effects",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/4/claim/25",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/4",
      "kind": "UNKNOWN",
      "text": "annual_count_of_mlb_hitting_and_pitching_coach_changes",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/4/claim/26",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/4",
      "kind": "UNKNOWN",
      "text": "completeness_of_public_coaching_staff_histories",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/4/claim/27",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/4",
      "kind": "UNKNOWN",
      "text": "availability_of_public_minor_league_staff_assignments_by_season",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/4/claim/28",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/4",
      "kind": "UNKNOWN",
      "text": "cubs_current_coaching_staff_vacancies_october_2026",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/4/claim/29",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/4",
      "kind": "UNKNOWN",
      "text": "cubs_existing_internal_coach_evaluation_methods",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/4/claim/30",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/4",
      "kind": "UNKNOWN",
      "text": "whether_other_clubs_already_use_coach_effect_models",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/4/claim/31",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/4",
      "kind": "UNKNOWN",
      "text": "minimum_sample_needed_to_distinguish_coach_ranking_from_reputation_baseline",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/5/claim/1",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/5",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Problem: building the postseason roster. Owner: GM and manager, with input from the analytics and pitching staff. Decision: who fills the 26 spots for each round, set before each series and reset between rounds, about 1 to 4 times per year when the club qualifies.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/5/claim/2",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/5",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Value at stake: in October one marginal win carries far more championship probability and revenue than a regular-season win, so small roster gains may be worth more than their run value suggests.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/5/claim/3",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/5",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Mechanism: short series with off-days need fewer starters and favor high-leverage relief depth, platoon bats against a known small set of opposing pitchers, and specialists such as a pinch runner or defensive replacement whose regular-season value was low.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/5/claim/4",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/5",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Baseline: carry the top 26 players by regular-season value, then adjust by staff judgment for health and matchups.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/5/claim/5",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/5",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Intervention: a series-specific simulator. Inputs are the public opponent rotation and bullpen, the off-day schedule, and public platoon and pitch-type splits. Output is the expected series win probability for each candidate roster compared with the baseline roster.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/5/claim/6",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/5",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Retrospective test: rebuild past postseason rosters league-wide from public transaction records and box scores, then score the alternatives a simulator would have recommended against the rosters actually used.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/5/claim/7",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/5",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "The difference in series win probability between a well-built roster and the baseline is large enough to measure. It may be well under one percentage point and lost in noise.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/5/claim/8",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/5",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "The 25th and 26th players get enough playing time in a series to matter. Postseason managers may concentrate innings on the top 8 to 10 pitchers regardless of roster choice.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/5/claim/9",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/5",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Contending clubs, including the Cubs, already run private versions of this simulation, so a public tool may only match current practice.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/5/claim/10",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/5",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Retrospective validation will suffer from very small samples, since each club plays few postseason series per decade. League-wide pooling is needed, and it removes club-specific context such as health.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/5/claim/11",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/5",
      "kind": "UNKNOWN",
      "text": "postseason_marginal_win_value_cubs",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/5/claim/12",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/5",
      "kind": "UNKNOWN",
      "text": "cubs_current_postseason_roster_process",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/5/claim/13",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/5",
      "kind": "UNKNOWN",
      "text": "public_injury_status_completeness_at_roster_deadline",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/5/claim/14",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/5",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Problem: setting up the late-season pitching rotation for the playoffs. Owner: manager and pitching coach, with front office input. Decision: in roughly the final 10 to 14 days, whether to keep using top starters to chase seeding or a bye, or to line them up for Game 1 of the Wild Card Series.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/5/claim/15",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/5",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Mechanism: weigh the change in odds of securing a bye or home field against the series win probability gained by starting the best pitcher in an elimination game. Feed live public standings and remaining schedules into a seeding simulation.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/5/claim/16",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/5",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Baseline: chase the best seed until it is clinched or out of reach, then line up the ace. Alternatively, rest regulars once the club has clinched.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/5/claim/17",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/5",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Retrospective test: from public game logs, reconstruct each contender's rotation choices in the final two weeks. Simulate alternative alignments using projected seeding odds as of each date, and compare.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/5/claim/18",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/5",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Rotation alignment changes series outcomes enough to matter. Pitcher quality gaps within a playoff rotation may be smaller than the value of a top seed.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/5/claim/19",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/5",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Public seeding-odds models are already widely used, so the advantage may lie only in combining seeding odds with rotation choices, not in either piece alone.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/5/claim/20",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/5",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Clubs may already handle this through staff judgment, and the decision is often forced by health or by how the race unfolds rather than chosen freely.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/5/claim/21",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/5",
      "kind": "UNKNOWN",
      "text": "magnitude_of_bye_value_under_current_playoff_format",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/5/claim/22",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/5",
      "kind": "UNKNOWN",
      "text": "how_often_cubs_face_this_decision_per_decade",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/5/claim/23",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/5",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Where software is likely unnecessary: legal roster eligibility and deadline rules for the postseason. Checklists and league office review already cover this, and the value is avoiding errors, not gaining an edge.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/5/claim/24",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-211812-efe1740f0c77/candidates/0/5",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Both ideas above may fail the objective's \"large enough to matter\" test because the decisions happen rarely. They are offered as a challenge to the preference for high-volume decisions, not as validated opportunities.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    }
  ],
  "evidence": [
    {
      "id": "objective_context",
      "text": "Where could software create a meaningful baseball advantage for the Chicago Cubs? The current date is early October 2026, in the Cubs' offseason (their 2026 season ended in the Wild Card Series). A prior experiment found that triaging the November minor-league free-agent pool offers little: the low-attention pool holds under one next-season contributor per club per year, and a simple 'played in MLB last year' rule already finds most value. Prefer recurring decisions where the value at stake is large enough to matter, where public information available at decision time could plausibly beat a simple rule, and where a retrospective test on public history is possible. Consider front office, player development, scouting, coaching and business-of-baseball decisions, and name where software is unnecessary or clubs are already ahead. OUTPUT GUIDANCE (format only): Each IDEA names one problem, the decision owner, the concrete recurring decision and its timing, the size of value at stake, the mechanism of advantage, the simple baseline a club already uses, and the software intervention. Follow with ASSUMPTION and UNKNOWN lines. Do not invent statistics or private Cubs information.",
      "facts": {},
      "provenance": {
        "source_type": "UNCLASSIFIED",
        "produced_by": "unknown",
        "source_ref": "",
        "independent_of_implementation": false,
        "represents_observed_reality": false
      }
    }
  ],
  "unresolved_assumptions": [
    "Public extension terms such as guarantees, option years and buyouts are reported completely and accurately enough to reconstruct contract value.",
    "The edge comes from timing and price, but the player's willingness to sign may dominate any club-side model.",
    "Clubs likely already run contract surplus models, so the marginal edge may be small.",
    "Public hearing outcomes, filing figures and settlements are recorded consistently across years.",
    "The number of hearings per year may be too small for a reliable model, which caps the edge.",
    "Specialized arbitration staff and outside firms likely already hold this knowledge, so clubs may be ahead.",
    "The non-tender market is predictable enough in size and quality from public information available in late November.",
    "This overlaps the roster-rules family, so it must show a distinct valuation edge to count as new.",
    "Public slot values and signed bonuses are available historically, but true asking prices are private, which limits the training labels.",
    "Career value from the draft takes years to observe, so a retrospective test may only validate bonus prediction, not talent selection.",
    "Most clubs already use pool-manipulation strategies, so the remaining edge may be thin.",
    "Public box-score-level college data covers enough games and opponents to estimate strength of schedule.",
    "Clubs with private college tracking data are likely already ahead, so this may matter only for low-coverage conferences.",
    "Like the minor-league free agent result, a \"recent MLB time\" rule may already capture most value, which would make this low-ceiling.",
    "Waiver priority and other clubs' claims limit the club's access to the top-ranked players.",
    "Public playoff-odds models are close enough to private ones that the edge lies in pricing discipline rather than better forecasts.",
    "Prospect value at trade time is hard to label retrospectively without hindsight bias.",
    "This may overlap the travel and rest planning family and must be framed specifically around day-night sequencing to be distinct.",
    "The effect may be too small or too noisy to detect in public data.",
    "Dynamic ticket pricing vendors already capture most of the available revenue edge for MLB clubs.",
    "Lineup-order optimization yields a marginal gain that is unlikely to justify new software.",
    "The current collective bargaining agreement expires around this offseason; this is unverified and must be confirmed.",
    "A retrospective test is only partly possible, by replaying past agreement transitions, which may be too few to validate.",
    "The QO decision may overlap previously explored arbitration or free-agent commitment families, so its novelty needs checking before investment.",
    "Public QO history has few cases per year, so a model may not separate from an experienced executive's judgment.",
    "The value of the compensation pick depends on the club's revenue-sharing and tax status under the CBA, which must be verified rather than assumed.",
    "The decision only recurs when the club qualifies, so annual expected value is discounted by playoff probability.",
    "Counterfactual roster value cannot be observed directly, so the retrospective test relies on simulation that may embed the same biases it is meant to test.",
    "Contending clubs likely already run such simulations internally, which would make the edge small.",
    "Coach effects may be confounded by roster turnover, front-office philosophy, and regression to the mean, making them unidentifiable from public data.",
    "Public staff records may be incomplete or inconsistently dated, especially for assistant and minor-league roles.",
    "This is unconventional precisely because it may not work, and a null result would itself be useful for avoiding overpaying for perceived coaching reputations.",
    "The per-attempt run value is small, so a season-level gain may be a fraction of a win.",
    "Leading clubs likely already exploit this, which would leave limited edge.",
    "Pitcher time-to-plate data may not be fully public, which would weaken the model.",
    "This may overlap the explored travel and rest planning family, which would need deduplication.",
